mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Oral and maxillofacial surgery is a field that primarily focuses on surgical treatments, with a focus on the study of oral organs (teeth, alveolar bone, lips, cheeks, tongue, palate, pharynx), facial soft tissues, jaw and face bones (maxilla, mandible, zygomatic bone), temporomandibular joint, salivary glands, and certain diseases in the neck. As an essential part of oral medicine, this discipline requires mastering basic skills such as examination and local anesthesia of the oral and maxillofacial region, dental and alveolar surgery, pre-restorative surgery, temporomandibular joint disorders, maxillofacial injuries, salivary gland diseases, maxillofacial nerve disorders, and maxillofacial infections. Additionally, it involves the treatment and operational skills for maxillofacial deformities, dental and maxillofacial deformities, and other maxillofacial plastic surgeries.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
